@startuml

title One export: every file is rebuilt from rows, and each owner is asked for its own

participant "ores.ore\nexport_run" as ops
participant "ores.reporting\nget_run_document" as rep
participant "ores.refdata and ores.analytics\nget a configuration document" as owners
participant "projection\nreverse / write" as proj

ops -> rep : the definition's run document
rep --> ops : configuration row and bindings
ops -> proj : reverse(run), then write
proj --> ops : ore.xml
loop each binding that names a document
    ops -> owners : configuration_id, party_id
    owners --> ops : rows
    ops -> proj : reverse(rows), then write
    proj --> ops : the document's text
end
ops --> ops : files keyed by the name the run document gave each one

note over ops
  A binding for the run settings or the engine settings produces no file:
  those rows are part of the run document, so they are written inside ore.xml.
end note

@enduml
